            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a newsreader, then the Marathi for to broadcast."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अफवा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अफवा — aphvā — \"a rumour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गावात भूकंपाची खोटी अफवा पसरली. gāvāt bhūkampācī khoṭī aphvā pasarlī. A false rumour of an earthquake spread through the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अफवा (aphvā) पसरणे, a rumour spreads; plural अफवा (aphvā)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अफवा (aphvā) is a loan from Persian afvāh, usually traced to Arabic afwāh, 'mouths': talk that goes from mouth to mouth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
